Thanks @stecasta — all four minors addressed in 07845a0:
- description now says two declaration sites (indexer + FlashInfer sparse);
- the settled `[64, 128]` note in the test is trimmed to a one-line comment;
- added `test_sm12x_default_launch_resolves_64_for_full_set`, which resolves the default through `Platform._preferred_block_size_for_backends` over the full DSv4.1 set (indexer, FlashInfer sparse, sparse SWA, compressor) and asserts 64 — the quantity the PR actually changes;
- the non-SM12x check is parametrized over SM90 (`[64]`) and SM100 (`[128]`).

Landing order stays as agreed: after #60948, or together with the #57292 guard.

